  "import_derivation": [
    "Static Calibri face lacks style:font-charset. Calc supplies osl_getThreadTextEncoding to XMLFontStylesContext; absent attribute retains signed16 thread default.",
    "Direct font-family without charset also injects signed16 current thread encoding in FontDefaultsCheck. Missing family instead inherits/defaults, which cannot be substituted for named Default Calibri11.",
    "x-symbol explicitly setsRTL_SYMBOL10. Other explicit tokens leave an empty Any and cannot be treated as a numeric default.",
    "Linux default encoding is codeset-derived: UTF8=>76, C ASCII codeset=>ISO8859_1=12, failed/unknown mapping=>ASCII_US11; a setter can override. Neither Calibri nor Swiss nor ODF absence fixes actual import-thread encoding."
  ],
  "native_derivation": [
    "Read exact UNO short as exact Python int; never normalize its stored observation.",
    "Signed short reconstructs uint16 as value modulo65536 after explicit named-profile membership.",
    "Lookup core table or full table. No encoding data yields Windowsbyte1; conditional full table alternatives are retained explicitly.",
    "BestWindows byte is converted by explicit native inverse switch. Windows0 ->RTL_MS1252=1; Windows1 ->defaultRTL_DONTKNOW=0.",
    "Candidate admits exactly32 named input encodings whose roundtrip is build-independent and exportRTL is0or1;66 other named encodings, reserved9, unassigned/user-range values remain outside this ordinary export profile.",
    "No-table enum font-charset inputs are not asserted to support a text converter; their exact native font export fallback is modelled explicitly."
  ],
